msgid "Turn the kill switch off to restore normal access without connecting."
msgstr "Turn the kill switch off to restore normal access without connecting."

#. Settings, kill switch: Disconnect always restores the internet; the switch only covers drops the user did not ask for.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_deliberate"
msgid "Pressing Disconnect always restores your internet straight away. The kill switch only applies to drops you did not ask for - a tunnel that stops carrying traffic, a network change, or the URnetwork service stopping."
msgstr "Pressing Disconnect always restores your internet straight away. The kill switch only applies to drops you did not ask for - a tunnel that stops carrying traffic, a network change, or the URnetwork service stopping."

#. Settings, kill switch: what may leave the device while the switch is on, and the name-lookup window during a connection attempt.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_dns_window"
msgid "While it is on and nothing is connecting, nothing leaves this device - name lookups included. During a connection attempt, name lookups from any app on this device can leave in the clear so URnetwork can reach its servers; everything else stays blocked."
msgstr "While it is on and nothing is connecting, nothing leaves this device - name lookups included. During a connection attempt, name lookups from any app on this device can leave in the clear so URnetwork can reach its servers; everything else stays blocked."

#. Settings: explanation under the kill switch switch.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_note"
msgid "If the tunnel drops unexpectedly, block this device's traffic instead of letting it out unprotected."
msgstr "If the tunnel drops unexpectedly, block this device's traffic instead of letting it out unprotected."

#. Kill switch: how to remove a block that is still in place when the device cannot reach the network; {command} is the shell command.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_recovery"
msgid "If this device cannot reach the network, a block installed earlier may still be in place; remove it with: {}"
msgstr "If this device cannot reach the network, a block installed earlier may still be in place; remove it with: {}"

#. Kill switch status: in force and armed, only local traffic leaves until connected.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_state_armed"
msgid "In force: nothing but local network traffic leaves this device until you connect."
msgstr "In force: nothing but local network traffic leaves this device until you connect."

#. Kill switch status: in force while connected, traffic is blocked if the tunnel drops.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_state_connected"
msgid "In force: if the tunnel drops, this device's traffic is blocked instead of going out unprotected."
msgstr "In force: if the tunnel drops, this device's traffic is blocked instead of going out unprotected."

#. Kill switch status: the system service could not install the block.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_state_failed"
msgid "The URnetwork system service could not install the kill switch, so your traffic is NOT being blocked."
msgstr "The URnetwork system service could not install the kill switch, so your traffic is NOT being blocked."

#. Kill switch status: not in force, traffic is not blocked.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_state_not_in_force"
msgid "The kill switch is NOT in force: your traffic is not being blocked."
msgstr "The kill switch is NOT in force: your traffic is not being blocked."

#. Kill switch status: nothing is blocked yet, takes effect on connect.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_state_pending"
msgid "Nothing is blocked yet — this takes effect the moment you connect."
msgstr "Nothing is blocked yet — this takes effect the moment you connect."

#. Kill switch status: the switch is off but the service still has a block installed, so traffic is blocked.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_state_still_installed"
msgid "The kill switch is off, but the URnetwork system service still has a block installed, so this device's traffic is being blocked."
msgstr "The kill switch is off, but the URnetwork system service still has a block installed, so this device's traffic is being blocked."

#. Kill switch status: cannot be checked right now.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_state_unknown"
msgid "Whether the kill switch is in force cannot be checked right now."
msgstr "Whether the kill switch is in force cannot be checked right now."

#. Kill switch: how to clear a block the service still has installed; {command} is the shell command to use if toggling does not work.
msgctxt "adv_kill_switch_still_installed_fix"
msgid "Turning the kill switch on and then off again asks the service to clear it; if that does not work, remove it with: {}"
msgstr "Turning the kill switch on and then off again asks the service to clear it; if that does not work, remove it with: {}"

